  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "What is the result of dividing $\\frac{9}{{t}^{3}}$ by $\\frac{2}{t}?$",
  "worked_solution": "To compute\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{{t}^{3}}\u00f7\\frac{2}{t},\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{{t}^{3}}\u00f7\\frac{2}{t} & = \\\\ \\frac{9}{{t}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{t}{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{9t}{2{t}^{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{9\\cancel{t}}{2{t}^{2}\\cdot \\cancel{t}} & = \\\\ \\frac{9}{2{t}^{2}} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that in the final step, we canceled out a common factor of $t$ in the numerator and denominator.",
